2026-10-09T01:04:04.5002134Z -- Input staleness watchdog (item 12)
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5002449Z   ok   a fresh sensor reads normally
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5002952Z   ok   an over-age value is rejected
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5003816Z   ok   the rejected value is still available for a graceful fallback
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5004558Z   ok   the age is reported so a user can see why
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5005223Z   ok   an outdoor reading may be older than an indoor one
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5005870Z   ok   the watchdog can be switched off entirely
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5006433Z   ok   the age limit can be relaxed
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5006953Z   ok   a future-stamped state is stale, not age 0
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5007361Z   ok   a 4 h backward host-clock step flags the reading stale
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5007751Z   ok   unavailable is distinguished from stale
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5008094Z   ok   a missing entity is reported as such
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5008430Z   ok   an unconfigured input is not a problem
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5008766Z   ok   a non-numeric state does not raise
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5009152Z   ok   a non-finite state string is refused exactly like a word
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5009597Z   ok   a non-finite value is refused after unit conversion too
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5010183Z   ok   the °F path itself keeps working (null control for the guard above)
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5010657Z   ok   an untimestamped state is used rather than discarded
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5011022Z   ok   stale inputs are listed
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5011307Z   ok   missing inputs are listed
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5011598Z   ok   the summary is human-readable
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5011895Z   ok   the evidence names the entity
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5012196Z   ok   the failing entity ids are listed
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5012573Z   ok   each failure reads as one line naming entity and class
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5012933Z   ok   watts are converted to kW
