2026-10-09T01:04:04.5854533Z   ok   all six transition days align prices to real instants
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5854666Z   ok   the plain day stays a zero null
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5854879Z   ok   _forecast_arrays and _price_series agree on the spring grid
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5855046Z   ok   _Horizon.timestamps invents no spring phantom
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5855267Z   ok   one horizon clock: the coordinator's import IS the optimizer's
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5855459Z   ok   coordinator and optimizer stamp the same spring grid
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5855665Z   ok   and on a step that is not a whole number of minutes (spring)
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5855848Z   ok   coordinator and optimizer stamp the same autumn grid
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5856046Z   ok   and on a step that is not a whole number of minutes (autumn)
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5856248Z   ok   spring and autumn UTC gaps are 15 minutes, plain day too
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5856414Z   ok   spring plan books no energy on a phantom step
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5856572Z   ok   autumn plan max gap is one 15-minute step
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5856580Z 
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5856817Z -- window_factors across a transition INSIDE the horizon (#777)
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5857037Z   ok   the transition really is inside the autumn and spring horizons
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5857266Z   ok   autumn fold: every window bills under the hour the meter keys it at
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5857495Z   ok   spring gap: every window bills under the hour the meter keys it at
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5857724Z   ok   NULL CONTROL: the ordinary Saturday a week earlier never disagreed
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5858011Z   ok   and the comparison is not vacuous — both rates occur in every cell
2026-10-09T01:04:04.5858020Z 
